<!-- Pull quote + body on why an odd table. -->
<section class="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="why-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why five</p>
        <p class="pull">
          Four people is two dates in the same room. Six is three. Five is a
          dinner party.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="body">
          An odd number has no clean way to pair off. The table keeps
          rearranging itself all night — someone turns to the person on their
          left, then the conversation swings back across the table, and nobody
          spends two hours locked into the wrong seatmate.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          It also means the night can't turn into a contest. There's no round
          where anyone gets sent home and no moment where the table watches you
          get picked or passed over. The only thing that happens in public is
          dinner.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          We build each table by hand — five people who can actually hold an
          evening together, on a night all five said they were free.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
